Review KB and TC independently. Keep critical trial issues open until the
required trial evidence supports closure. Track unresolved decisions and
environment blockers without treating their presence in a log as closure or
readiness.

For project review, gather actual requirements, product behavior, original
acceptance and effective approvals. Gather module, interface, data, state,
dependency and candidate designs, target platform and installation,
signing and upgrade boundaries, and available test environments. Keep the
critical assumptions, thresholds, scale, trials, API and credential
responsibilities, permission, outbound and cost boundaries, and knowledge
versions, adoption, authorization and citations explicit. Retain actual
source, packages, UI, file and failure evidence and the verification report
as applicable. Record missing material with its current status and intended
use.

The source provenance retains historical demonstrations and reading indexes.
Use demonstrations as method examples and record project decisions and
results from actual evidence. Apply thresholds, budgets and approval
procedures from effective project requirements.
